  <data key="d2">The Engineering, Procurement, and Construction (EPC) model, also known as 工程总承包模式, is a comprehensive project delivery system widely utilized in the international engineering construction field. This model encompasses the entire lifecycle of a project, including planning, engineering, procurement, construction, and commissioning. It allows for a single point of responsibility, where a single entity or a consortium takes on the complete responsibility for the project. The EPC model is characterized by its integration of design, procurement, and construction services, streamlining the process and reducing complexity. It is recognized as a mainstream project management approach, offering companies a cohesive and efficient way to manage projects. This model is particularly effective in ensuring a seamless transition from design to construction, as it consolidates all project phases into one contract.&lt;SEP&gt;A project delivery method known as Engineering, Procurement, and Construction (EPC)总承包模式.&lt;SEP&gt;工程总承包模式是指一种项目交付方式，包括设计、采购和施工。&lt;SEP&gt;Engineering procurement construction (EPC) model, a method for infrastructure development.</data>
