<node id="北斗七星框架">
  <data key="d0">北斗七星框架</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Beidou Seven Stars framework, also known as the Big Dipper framework, is an innovative strategic analysis tool designed to evaluate and guide the strategic layout, business composition, support system, innovation path, and risk challenges of various entities, with a particular focus on the EPC (Engineering, Procurement, and Construction) business of Hualu Company. This framework, which draws upon the refined practices of SGECL in EPC project management, is composed of seven core elements that represent the company's seven key capabilities: strategic leadership, market insight, technological innovation, project management, resource integration, risk control, and talent support. Beyond its application within Hualu Company, the Beidou Seven Stars framework serves as a strategic recommendation at the national think tank level, aiming to assist entities in building a sustained competitive advantage and leading the new era of engineering construction. It has been applied to analyze the strategic layout and business composition of the Shandong Institute, showcasing its versatility across different contexts. The framework is recognized as an analysis model and theoretical model for examining the micro-project management practices of CPECC and is also considered an analysis tool and model within the context of this report. It is a comprehensive framework analyzing the comprehensive strength and development level of enterprises from seven key dimensions.</data>
