<node id="EPC模式">
  <data key="d0">EPC模式</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The EPC模式, also known as the Engineering, Procurement, and Construction model, is an integrated service and engineering总承包 mode that encompasses design, procurement, and construction. This model is designed to integrate various professional resources, ensuring system coordination and optimization throughout the entire project lifecycle. It is characterized by the consolidation of design, procurement, and construction phases into a unified organizational approach, which facilitates systemic integration and optimization. The EPC mode is widely applied in China's construction sector, being the most prevalent engineering总承包 model in the field. It represents a progressive engineering construction organization model that has gained significant traction in the industry. The EPC model is a project delivery system where one company is responsible for the entire project, including engineering, procurement, and construction. This method is known for its responsibility clarity, risk control, and ease of financing. The model describes an engineering总承包 mode that includes design, procurement, construction, and operation and maintenance. The EPC mode is utilized in various industries, including the construction and electric power sectors. It is a method of engineering, procurement, and construction that integrates design, procurement, and construction into a unified process, with the总承包商 coordinating and managing all stages of the project.</data>
