<node id="EPC总承包模式">
  <data key="d0">EPC总承包模式</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The EPC总承包模式, also known as the Engineering, Procurement, and Construction (EPC) model, is a comprehensive approach to project management that integrates the design, procurement, and construction phases of a project into a single, cohesive phase. This method is characterized by a single contract with a general contractor, which streamlines the project delivery process by reducing risks, concurrent project phases, and design changes. The EPC总承包 mode extends beyond the traditional EPC model, incorporating a broader framework that includes policy, asset investment, construction, operation, and research. It is widely adopted in international engineering contracting and is considered a mainstream trend in the field of engineering construction. Under the owner's delegation, the general contractor is responsible for the comprehensive management of engineering, procurement, construction, quality, safety, progress, and cost, typically utilized in large industrial projects. This mode effectively controls quality, progress, and cost, and is known for its holistic approach to project management.</data>
