  <data key="d2">Sustainable development refers to the practice of meeting the needs of the present without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs. This concept emphasizes the balance between economic growth, social equity, and environmental protection. It is defined as the ability to maintain long-term viability and prosperity, ensuring that current demands are met without damaging the resources and environment necessary for future generations to thrive. Sustainable development is not only a principle but also a strategy for businesses and organizations to adopt, as it involves aspects such as green construction, employee care, community contributions, and transparent governance. This approach is crucial for building a responsible corporate citizenship image and fostering a sustainable future.&lt;SEP&gt;Sustainable development&lt;SEP&gt;满足当前需求而不损害未来世代需求的发展模式&lt;SEP&gt;The ability of a company to develop in a way that meets the needs of the present without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Sustainable development, a process that aims to meet the needs of the present without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs.</data>
