<node id="EPC项目">
  <data key="d0">EPC项目</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The EPC项目, or Engineering, Procurement, and Construction project, refers to an integrated project model that encompasses the entire scope of engineering, procurement, and construction activities. Typically, EPC projects are associated with large-scale construction projects, such as infrastructure and buildings. These projects are characterized by a single point of responsibility for the design, procurement, and construction phases, which can lead to more efficient project management and cost control. The EPC model has been successfully applied in various sectors, including the construction of pump storage power stations and offshore wind farms, where it has contributed to significant breakthroughs, as evidenced by the achievements of Central South Institute. The term "EPC项目" is also used in a broader context to describe projects managed under the EPC总承包 mode, involving the coordination of engineering, procurement, and construction activities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-cd98fa71ea0655e21fa0a2276d13a0d9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0f4f29c7c713a0dc9cceab37367c4fc5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-672521f12fd1986bcd639d9767739595-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aad98ed6151be31033f17cc129b4d0a9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b25c2bf361b1d3a2ceed0acc32ff9c3b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c624410f178b887c6c0457b877b38623-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c7786e670e089b87df36cc29f6ebd44e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c7786e670e089b87df36cc29f6ebd44e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c7786e670e089b87df36cc29f6ebd44e-chunk-003</data>
